  <main>

    <!-- ── Act 1: Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="hv2-hero" data-act="hero" aria-labelledby="hv2-h1">
      <div class="hv2-hero-inner">
        <div class="hv2-hero-text">
          <h1 class="hv2-h1" id="hv2-h1">Reliable web <span class="hv2-parse" data-parse data-parse-glyphs="/home/parse-word-glyphs.js" data-parse-ink="--zen-teal-5">data</span> when the web fights back.</h1>
          <p class="hv2-sub">Web data infrastructure for AI agents, data, and automation teams. Fetch, extract, crawl, batch, or drive a browser, all through one platform.</p>
          <div class="hv2-hero-ctas">
            <a class="btn-marketing" href="https://app.zenrows.com/register">Start free</a>
            <button class="btn-marketing btn-marketing--secondary hero-add" type="button" data-copy-skill aria-label="Copy the setup prompt for your agent">
              <span class="hero-add-roll">
                <span class="hero-add-track">
                  <span class="hero-add-line">Add to your agent</span>
                  <span class="hero-add-line" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="hero-add-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3.2L13 5" /></svg>Copied</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="cta-stack-tag">5,000 free credits/month, always. No card.</p>
          <p class="hero-add-hint" data-add-hint data-md-skip aria-live="polite">Paste it into your agent to finish setup <span class="hero-add-hint-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></p>
          <!-- Live-scale proof. Three figures, no chrome, each proving a different
               thing: how much the gateway carries, how much of the web it gets
               into, and the uptime a third party measured. Only two of them are
               numbers; the middle one is a coverage claim, and it is deliberate
               that it does not try to be a count.

               The request figure is the approved public traffic claim, +10B a
               month, set by marketing (2026-09-04) and stated as a floor so it
               stays true as the month rolls rather than needing a rewrite.
               Uptime is the Fetch component on status.zenrows.com. The systems
               slot is the one qualitative figure and reads as an unqualified
               absolute by explicit decision (marketing, 2026-09-04), taken with
               the governance rule in view: the SOT claims list (§13) puts
               "bypass all anti-bot" under MUST avoid, and /bypass itself, which
               this links to, says "Every major anti-bot system, handled
               automatically". The qualifier was dropped on purpose, so treat
               this as a decision to raise rather than a slip to quietly fix,
               and restore "major" if the call is reversed. The volume and
               uptime figures both link to where a reader can check them.

               Gone from here: a per-second rate. It read 369/s, derived from the
               gateway measurement the volume used to quote. Once the volume
               became an approved claim rather than a log read, the two could
               only agree by dividing one into the other, which is arithmetic
               wearing the clothes of evidence. A third number has to prove a
               third thing.

               Deliberately NOT here: a success rate. The gateway puts it in the
               sixties on the raw denominator and the low eighties on the most
               generous one, so any figure would either be unflattering or need a
               denominator nobody has agreed on. The three that are here need no
               caveat. -->
          <!-- The proof row lives in the text column, under the CTAs, at every
               size (2026-10-03): pinned to the foot of the hero it fell below the
               fold once the primitive stage grew, and on one-column layouts it
               landed under the stage. Here it is always on the first screen. -->
          <ul class="hv2-proof" aria-label="Scale, coverage and reliability">
            <li>
              <span class="hv2-proof-n">10B+</span>
              <span class="hv2-proof-l">requests a month</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/bypass">
                <span class="hv2-proof-n">All</span>
                <span class="hv2-proof-l">anti-bot systems, handled</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://status.zenrows.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span class="hv2-proof-n">100%</span>
                <span class="hv2-proof-l">Fetch uptime, 90 days</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- One page, five ways to get it. The hero's visual is a single
             product page and the primitives are lenses over it: Fetch reads it
             into Markdown, Extract lifts its fields into JSON, Crawl walks its
             links and lists every page it finds, Batch makes it one of many in
             a job, Browser drives it. The page stays
             the protagonist, so this does not clone Act 3's product cards.
             Data-driven (home.js HP_MODES): a primitive is one entry there
             plus one tab here (Crawl joined that way on its launch, 2026-10-09). Icons are the app's
             own Rive files from its primitive tabs (_assets/primitives). -->
        <div class="hp" data-hp>
          <div class="seg-control seg-control--md hp-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Zenrows primitives">
            <button class="seg-control-opt hp-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="hp-tab-fetch" aria-controls="hp-scene" aria-selected="true" data-hp-mode="fetch"><canvas class="hp-ic" data-prim="fetch" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Fetch</button>
            <button class="seg-control-opt hp-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="hp-tab-extract" aria-controls="hp-scene" aria-selected="false" data-hp-mode="extract"><canvas class="hp-ic" data-prim="extract" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Extract</button>
            <button class="seg-control-opt hp-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="hp-tab-crawl" aria-controls="hp-scene" aria-selected="false" data-hp-mode="crawl"><canvas class="hp-ic" data-prim="crawl" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Crawl</button>
            <button class="seg-control-opt hp-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="hp-tab-batch" aria-controls="hp-scene" aria-selected="false" data-hp-mode="batch"><canvas class="hp-ic" data-prim="batch" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Batch</button>
            <button class="seg-control-opt hp-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="hp-tab-browser" aria-controls="hp-scene" aria-selected="false" data-hp-mode="browser"><canvas class="hp-ic" data-prim="browser" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Browser</button>
          </div>
          <div class="hp-scene" id="hp-scene" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="hp-tab-fetch" data-mode="fetch">
            <div class="hp-box">
            <div class="hp-page panel" aria-hidden="true" data-kind="colour">
              <div class="hp-bar"><span class="hp-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="hp-url" data-hp-url>auroraaudio.shop/p/aurora-headphones</span><span class="hp-cart" data-hp-cart></span></div>
              <div class="hp-body">
                <div class="hp-img"><picture class="hp-shot is-on" data-hp-shot="0"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-0.avif" type="image/avif"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-0.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/home/hero/ecommerce-0.jpg" width="720" height="900" alt="" loading="eager" decoding="async"></picture><picture class="hp-shot" data-hp-shot="1"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-1.avif" type="image/avif"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-1.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/home/hero/ecommerce-1.jpg" width="720" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture><picture class="hp-shot" data-hp-shot="2"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-2.avif" type="image/avif"><source srcset="/home/hero/ecommerce-2.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="/home/hero/ecommerce-2.jpg" width="720" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture></div>
                <div class="hp-info">
                  <span class="hp-line" style="--w:38%"></span>
                  <span class="hp-f hp-f--title" data-f="0">Aurora Wireless Headphones</span>
                  <span class="hp-f hp-f--rating" data-f="1">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9734; 4.6</span>
                  <span class="hp-row"><span class="hp-f hp-f--price" data-f="2">$149.00</span><span class="hp-f hp-f--stock" data-f="3">In stock</span></span>
                  <span class="hp-swatches"><i data-hp-swatch="0"></i><i data-hp-swatch="1"></i><i data-hp-swatch="2"></i></span>
                  <span class="hp-buy" data-hp-buy></span>
                  <span class="hp-line" style="--w:92%"></span>
                  <span class="hp-line" style="--w:84%"></span>
                  <span class="hp-line" style="--w:66%"></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <span class="hp-scan"></span>
              <!-- The film cursor (video/src/lib/cursor.tsx): a notchless quad
                   whose fat round-joined stroke rounds every corner, teal-to-
                   purple body, light halo, soft shadow. Pablo, 2026-10-03:
                   bring the film's gradient cursor to this stage (the motion
                   skill keeps it film-only unless he asks). -->
              <span class="hp-ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="hp-cursor" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="hp-cursor-arrow" viewBox="-3 -3 30 30">
                <defs>
                  <linearGradient id="hp-cur-g" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--zen-teal-5)"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--zen-purple-6)"/></linearGradient>
                  <filter id="hp-cur-sh" x="-40%" y="-40%" width="180%" height="180%" color-interpolation-filters="sRGB"><feDropShadow dx="0" dy="2.2" stdDeviation="2.4" flood-color="#1D1612" flood-opacity="0.4"/></filter>
                </defs>
                <g filter="url(#hp-cur-sh)">
